      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Organisation’s experts say pledge puts pressure on UK public finances and ‘adds significant fiscal risks’</p><p>Labour should ditch the triple-lock pensions promise to help tackle the UK’s straitened public finances, the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development has urged.</p><p>In its latest survey of the UK economy, the Paris-based club of industrialised nations added its voice to those calling for an end to the pledge, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2025/sep/16/uk-state-pension-what-is-the-triple-lock-and-could-it-be-ditched\">which uprates the state pension each year</a> by whichever is the highest of wage growth, inflation or 2.5%.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/15/labour-should-ditch-triple-lock-pensions-promise-says-oecd\">Continue reading...</a>"
